{"timestamp": "2026-10-13T16:13:01+00:00", "question": "What should staff do when a sales rep pushes a today-only discount?", "retrieved": [{"label": "S1", "chunk_id": "GDE-01#the-problem", "score": 16.43}, {"label": "S2", "chunk_id": "GDE-01#what-staff-should-do", "score": null}, {"label": "S3", "chunk_id": "SUP-01#ordering-and-minimum-order", "score": 3.17}, {"label": "S4", "chunk_id": "SUP-01#delivery", "score": null}, {"label": "S5", "chunk_id": "GDE-01#gifts", "score": null}], "model": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "answer": "Staff should never agree to an order on the spot, as they have no authority to place orders [S2]. They should ask the representative to send a written quotation to the owner and use the AI assistant's figures as evidence to decline the offer if stock levels are sufficient [S2]. Additionally, staff should report repeated pressure from a supplier to the owner [S2].", "check": {"cited": [2], "invalid": [], "is_refusal": false, "citations_ok": true}, "sources": [{"label": "S1", "chunk_id": "GDE-01#the-problem", "title": "Guidance: Handling Supplier Pressure", "section": "The problem", "source": "knowledge/corpus/GDE-01_handling-supplier-pressure.md"}, {"label": "S2", "chunk_id": "GDE-01#what-staff-should-do", "title": "Guidance: Handling Supplier Pressure", "section": "What staff should do", "source": "knowledge/corpus/GDE-01_handling-supplier-pressure.md"}, {"label": "S3", "chunk_id": "SUP-01#ordering-and-minimum-order", "title": "Supplier Profile: Kampala Office Supplies", "section": "Ordering and minimum order", "source": "knowledge/corpus/SUP-01_kampala-office-supplies.md"}, {"label": "S4", "chunk_id": "SUP-01#delivery", "title": "Supplier Profile: Kampala Office Supplies", "section": "Delivery", "source": "knowledge/corpus/SUP-01_kampala-office-supplies.md"}, {"label": "S5", "chunk_id": "GDE-01#gifts", "title": "Guidance: Handling Supplier Pressure", "section": "Gifts", "source": "knowledge/corpus/GDE-01_handling-supplier-pressure.md"}]}
